# Dash AI API — STAGING FIRST BRING-UP overlay (no paid inference, no push).
#
# Apply these values ON TOP OF staging.env.example for the first staging deployment and every
# smoke run until the owner approves live providers. With them the server:
#   - starts in production mode without any AI provider key (no OpenAI, Anthropic, Bedrock or
#     compatible-provider credential is needed, and none should be copied into staging for this step);
#   - answers with the two built-in demonstration adapters only: nothing is sent to any provider,
#     every ledger row is priced "demo" at 0 USD, and provider keys present by mistake are ignored;
#   - logs two expected start-up warnings, both starting "PROVIDER_MODE=fake" (no other warning);
#   - sends no push notifications (no Firebase credential needed).
# Leaving the live staging.env.example values instead would make the server refuse to start without
# real provider keys and spend limits: that is the intended fail-closed behaviour, not a bug to work around.
# A test (apps/api/test/unit.test.ts) keeps this overlay valid. See docs/staging-runbook.md §4.

PROVIDER_MODE=fake
PAID_PROVIDERS_ENABLED=false
FREE_POOL_ENABLED=false
BEDROCK_ENABLED=false
COMPATIBLE_PROVIDERS=
PUSH_TRANSPORT=none
